---
import TreatmentPage from "../../../components/TreatmentPage.astro";

const T = "/services/fertility-treatment";

// NOTE: Copy deliberately covers PGT for medical and genetic indications only.
// It does not target "gender selection" keywords. Confirm clinic policy before adding any.

const page = {
  slug: "pgt",
  name: "Embryo Genetic Testing (PGT)",
  title: "PGT Embryo Genetic Testing in Lahore | PGT-A & PGT-M",
  description:
    "PGT in Lahore: what PGT-A, PGT-M and PGT-SR are, who may benefit, how embryo biopsy works, limitations and cost. Honest guidance from Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  eyebrow: "Embryo Genetic Testing",
  h1: "PGT Embryo Genetic Testing in Lahore",
  waText: "Hello, I would like to ask about PGT embryo genetic testing with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  ctaLabel: "Book a PGT consultation",
  heroSub: [
    "Preimplantation genetic testing (PGT) checks embryos created through IVF for specific chromosomal or inherited conditions before one is transferred to the uterus. It was previously known as PGD and PGS.",
    "At Kamran Fertility Clinic, Dr. Kamran Saleem explains who may genuinely benefit from PGT, what it can and cannot tell you, and why it is not needed in every IVF cycle.",
  ].join(" "),
  leadIn: [
    { rich: ["PGT is only possible within an ", ["IVF", `${T}/ivf`], " or ", ["ICSI", `${T}/icsi`], " cycle, so it is usually discussed as part of a wider treatment plan."] },
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      id: "what-is-pgt",
      title: "What Is PGT (Preimplantation Genetic Testing)?",
      intro: "PGT examines a few cells from an embryo before transfer.",
      icon: "flask",
      body: [
        "After IVF, embryos are grown to the blastocyst stage, around day five or six. A few cells are carefully removed from the outer layer, which will become the placenta, and sent to a specialist genetics laboratory. Meanwhile the embryo is frozen. Results guide which embryo is transferred in a later frozen cycle.",
        "You may still see the older names PGD (preimplantation genetic diagnosis) and PGS (preimplantation genetic screening). PGD is now generally called PGT-M or PGT-SR, and PGS is called PGT-A.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "types-of-pgt",
      title: "Types of PGT: PGT-A, PGT-M and PGT-SR",
      intro: "The type of test depends on the question being asked.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "PGT-A (aneuploidy screening): counts the chromosomes in an embryo, since embryos with extra or missing chromosomes often fail to implant or miscarry.",
          "PGT-M (monogenic conditions): tests for a specific inherited disease, such as thalassemia or cystic fibrosis, when one or both parents carry the gene.",
          "PGT-SR (structural rearrangements): checks embryos when a parent carries a balanced chromosomal translocation or inversion.",
        ] },
        "Embryo sex is reported only where it is medically relevant, such as in X-linked disorders.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "who-may-benefit-from-pgt",
      title: "Who May Benefit From PGT?",
      intro: "PGT is considered where there is a specific, identifiable reason.",
      icon: "user",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Couples who carry a known inherited condition",
          "A parent with a balanced chromosomal rearrangement",
          "A previous pregnancy or child affected by a genetic or chromosomal condition",
          "Recurrent miscarriage, in selected cases after investigation",
          "Repeated unexplained implantation failure, selectively",
        ] },
        "For most couples having IVF for other reasons, PGT-A has not been shown to improve the chance of a live birth, and professional bodies urge caution about offering it routinely. It may reduce the number of embryos available to transfer, and can discard embryos that might have produced a healthy baby.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "pgt-process-step-by-step",
      title: "The PGT Process, Step by Step",
      intro: "PGT adds laboratory steps and usually a frozen transfer to an IVF cycle.",
      icon: "calendar",
      body: [
        { h3: "1. Genetic counseling and test planning" },
        "Carrier status, family history and previous results are reviewed, and a suitable test is chosen. For PGT-M, the genetics laboratory often needs time to prepare a test specific to your family.",
        { h3: "2. IVF with ICSI" },
        "Stimulation, egg retrieval and fertilization follow as in IVF. ICSI is usually used to avoid contamination from extra sperm DNA.",
        { h3: "3. Embryo culture and biopsy" },
        "Embryos are grown to the blastocyst stage and a few cells are biopsied. Embryos are then frozen.",
        { h3: "4. Genetic analysis" },
        "The biopsy is analyzed in a specialist laboratory. Results usually take about one to two weeks.",
        { h3: "5. Frozen embryo transfer" },
        { rich: ["An embryo with a favorable result is transferred in a later ", ["FET cycle", `${T}/fet`], ". Prenatal testing in pregnancy is still advised to confirm the result."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "pgt-limitations",
      title: "What PGT Cannot Do",
      intro: "PGT reduces uncertainty. It does not remove it.",
      icon: "shield",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "It cannot guarantee a pregnancy or a healthy baby",
          "It tests only for the conditions or chromosomes it is designed to detect, not every genetic disorder",
          "A few cells may not represent the whole embryo, and mosaic results are hard to interpret",
          "False positive and false negative results are possible, so confirmatory prenatal testing is recommended",
          "It involves extra laboratory handling and cost",
        ] },
        "Dr. Kamran will give you an honest assessment of whether PGT is likely to help in your situation, including when it is not recommended.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "pgt-risks",
      title: "Risks and Considerations",
      intro: "Embryo biopsy is performed by experienced embryologists, but it is not risk-free.",
      icon: "heart",
      body: [
        "The biopsy carries a small theoretical risk of damaging the embryo. PGT also usually means fewer embryos to transfer, and some couples find they have no embryo suitable for transfer in a given cycle. All the usual IVF risks apply, including hyperstimulation and multiple pregnancy.",
        "Ethical and legal rules around embryo testing differ between countries. In Pakistan, PGT is offered for medical and genetic indications.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "pgt-cost-in-lahore",
      title: "PGT Cost in Lahore",
      intro: "PGT is an additional cost on top of IVF.",
      icon: "coin",
      body: [
        "The total depends on the type of test, the number of embryos biopsied, the genetics laboratory fee, frozen transfer costs and storage. PGT-M may also need a test developed for your family's specific variant. You will receive an itemized estimate during your consultation.",
      ],
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: "What is PGT in IVF?", a: "PGT (preimplantation genetic testing) checks embryos created through IVF for chromosomal or inherited conditions before one is chosen for transfer." },
    { q: "What is the difference between PGD and PGS?", a: "These are older names. PGD is now called PGT-M or PGT-SR (testing for a specific inherited condition or a chromosomal rearrangement), and PGS is called PGT-A (screening for extra or missing chromosomes)." },
    { q: "Does everyone having IVF need PGT?", a: "No. PGT is considered when there is a specific reason, such as a known genetic condition. For most patients having IVF, routine PGT-A has not been shown to improve live birth rates." },
    { q: "Is PGT accurate?", a: "PGT is accurate for what it tests, but it is not perfect. Mosaic embryos and laboratory limitations mean confirmatory prenatal testing is still advised." },
    { q: "Does PGT harm the embryo?", a: "The biopsy carries a small theoretical risk, but it is performed at the blastocyst stage by experienced embryologists. It is considered safe when done correctly." },
    { q: "How long do PGT results take?", a: "Usually about one to two weeks, which is why embryos are frozen and transferred in a later frozen cycle." },
    { q: "Can PGT guarantee a healthy baby?", a: "No. It reduces the risk of specific conditions, but it cannot test for everything and cannot guarantee pregnancy." },
  ],
  closingHeading: "PGT Embryo Genetic Testing With Dr. Kamran Saleem",
  closingParas: [
    "At Kamran Fertility Clinic, Dr. Kamran Saleem provides guidance on PGT for couples in Lahore, including whether it is likely to be of real benefit in your situation.",
    "Genetic testing is carried out by a specialist genetics laboratory, and we explain clearly what is done in the clinic, what is coordinated with partner services, and the limits of the results.",
  ],
  resources: [
    { href: "/resources/ivf-treatment-in-lahore", category: "Fertility Treatment", title: "IVF Treatment in Lahore: Cost, Process, Tests & Choosing the Right Clinic" },
    { href: "/resources/icsi-treatment-in-lahore", category: "Fertility Treatment", title: "ICSI Treatment in Lahore: Procedure, Cost, Benefits and Success Factors" },
  ],
  close: {
    heading: "Thinking About Genetic Testing?",
    body: "Bring any genetic reports, carrier results or previous miscarriage records to your consultation.",
    cta: "Book a PGT Consultation",
  },
};
---

<TreatmentPage {...page} />
